flowchart TD

    A[Method Call Occurs] --> B[Check All Aspects' Pointcuts]

%% Decision: does any pointcut match this method call?
    B -->|Match Found| C[Create JoinPoint represents the current method execution context]
    B -->|No Match| I[No AOP Interception; Proceed Normally]

%% If a match is found, we proceed with advice execution
C[JoinPoint Created] --> D[Execute 'before' Advice from the Matching Aspects]
D --> E[Invoke Original Method via JoinPoint]
E --> F[Execute 'after' Advice from Matching Aspects]
F --> G[Return Final Result to Caller]

%% If no match is found, we just execute the method as usual
I[No AOP Interception] --> G[Return Result]

%% Descriptions
%% Aspect: Defines Pointcuts and the associated Advice (before, after)
%% Pointcut: Expression that determines whether a JoinPoint (method call) is intercepted
%% Advice: Code that runs before, after, or around the JoinPoint execution
%% JoinPoint: Represents a specific execution instance of a method (including context like args, target object)
